Spell option presets ("depends" .p files) installed into the build chroot's
/etc/sorcery/local/depends/<spell>.p by cauldron_sorcerous_cauldron_defaults,
so unattended casts don't fall back to unsuitable defaults:

  locale      only en_US (+ en_US.UTF-8 and C.UTF-8) instead of all ~196
              locales (~130 MB); users pick their own with "cast -r locale"
  net-tools   don't stop to ask about network configuration
  python3     don't install the test suite (--disable-test-modules)

A preset replaces the spell's whole .p file, so list all of its options.

../default_depends is installed as the build chroot's
/var/state/sorcery/default_depends: default answers to optional dependencies
("spell:dependency:on|off", no comments allowed). Without an answer, sorcery
enables an optional dependency whenever it is installed in the build chroot,
which pulls in more than an install medium needs:

  nghttp2     no python bindings / boost (needed via cmake -> curl; would
              otherwise drag in boost and openmpi)
